031_torch_geometry reuse torch.cdist geometry for both coupling and point potentials, based023/029 (2/1 torch threads). All30 local screens valid max nrmse .0057770750, min rho .9999779964, min overlap .9933333. This removes repeated double SciPy distance geometry and float32 copy.\n\n032_numpy_dual based031 replaces ONLY point annealing updates by NumPy arrays, SciPy logsumexp, preserving cached Gibbs kernels, shared reduced-cost minima and symmetric finite schedule. This is a library/kernel implementation ablation, not a learned surrogate. Local screen pending. All sources and logs saved. No newly screened source is retained as final until full evaluation.\n\n023 full completed quality valid; raw .2590207737681339, score .503310747054841, exact reported source hash fb46e5d3b5dc019ba7d3858876ad64af9a951d943f9e5d0229b19707e0e99ad0. Quality max nrmse .0057769853, min rho .9999779964, min top .9933333. Full result archived023/result.json. This is current best, method.py remains023. Seed aggregates101 .23734,202 .32743,303 .28082,404 .23621,505 .21330 seconds; variability substantial.\n\n032 all30 local valid max nrmse .0057772001, min rank .9999780027, min top .9933333. 033_numpy_labels extends032 by moving masked batched class dual solves to NumPy/SciPy too; keeps Torch geometry/coupling. All30 local valid max nrmse .0057772199, min rank .9999780036, min top .9933333. Library implementations algebraically mirror the hybrid approximation; class geometry remains computed from inputs. Paired alternating bench_round_4 comparing023/029/030/031/032/033 without evaluator concurrency. Next fully evaluate fastest kernel implementation, keep only if aggregate improves.\n\nClean alternating bench_round_4 (no evaluator running) overturned the contended one-thread result: medians023 .21498,029 .25002,030 .18192,031 .25223,032 .39500,033 .38525 seconds. Use2 Torch threads. NumPy/SciPy general logsumexp is slower. Full030 evaluation started (Torch geometry reused, based023). 034_nu